maps.summary:
aether has the middle of the quant chain. It has:
- quants/head8: quant8, the 3,200-byte 3.1 KB tuple, ported, with the owner's benchmark and receipts.
- quants/hyperbehcs: slots 9-12.
- quants/exact: binary, hex and BEHCS rungs, the dbbh crate, the qprism-3d-slice-harness, and the 256↔1024 transcode as line ranges.
- quants/recovery: Path 1 and Path 2.
- quants/slice-time-harness.
- quants/cubes: Q-PRISM slot 21 plus slots 25, 26 and 28.
- qprism/: rust-qprism-181, the omega codecs and the throat.
- eval/vendor/qprism-control: the Q-PRISM Python package with alphabet-1024.
- The 3,174-byte keys, q_prisms.py and PLAY.md.
- The combined-quant registry, atlas and lattice .hbp.

What is missing is mostly the beginning:
- **The language layer the owner calls the alphabet, verbs and tuples:**
  - the IX/LX index language (IX-060 'the index IS a language', 425 agent-index files, 1 of them in aether) and the compiled agent index;
  - the 75-verb ix/grammar verb-table and verb-factory;
  - the 35D/47D hyperlanguage tuple catalog, where D2 is VERB;
  - the BEHCS codex 14-field tuple (tools/behcs-codex.js);
  - the IX-700 BEHCS-256 alphabet with its 47-catalog registry, plus codex-bridge;
  - GLYPH-GENESIS in its JS, TS and Rust glyph_genesis forms.

  All of these are in the Asolaria mirror or asolaria-behcs-256 and federation-1024, and none is in aether.
- **ACER-only quant engines.** These are known only from the ALGORITHMS-PID-REGISTRATION rows, which aether also lacks:
  - combined-quant-engine.mjs and its proof harness (2026-06-15);
  - extract-to-cube.mjs, the 3-level PRISM BEHCS256 → 1024 → HyperBEHCS;
  - hyperbehcsRepresentationAlgorithms.js, which the received hyperbehcsQuantSubstrate.js requires;
  - A12-OMNIQUANT-RUST (2026-05-20);
  - the substrate tuples codec.
- **The repeated quant-down receipts and harnesses:**
  - the reductions old-compression curve (JSON → tuple → verb-overlay → glyph, with anchors 12:1 / 21,141:1 / ~3B:1);
  - the HYPER-BECHS third-seat E8/E9 ladder, codec v0.1 and multilevel BPE;
  - the measured addendum;
  - ASOLARIA-AS-NEURAL-NETWORK's QUANT8DEFS, fidelity specs, zeta-quant and the D22 verb adapter;
  - the canon's 3.1 KB-class contract;
  - the universe simulator's RESULTS-5355 horizon recursion. That receipt itself says the 3.1 KB → exact-bytes loop was not run, and the recursion code is in no repository.
  - the RAINBOR exabyte funnel leaves, which say 1 EB goes to a few hundred bytes.
- **Q-PRISM's own first-commit files:** run_experiment.py, results/*, the two host8 Rust files whole, and its docs.
- **The Liris build** of Q-PRISM and the matter-wave proof, held on Liris only.
- **No receipt for '30 exabytes into 900 bytes'** exists in any of the 132 mirror refs (every blob scanned), the local estate, or the gap-work clones.

Read-only clones I made are under /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/b2fb539a-cb4d-5f0b-a22f-ca1a7fcb500d/scratchpad/gap-work/qprism/:
- qprism-organoid
- three *.hist.git (blobless)
- the LX-chain and IX-chain tokens-savings repos

The blob-scan output is in hits.tsv and firsts.tsv in the same folder.
